Arcanum CE patch 2 of 3 for innospect 0.2.0 (gogx, 2026-10-31).

Strings are UTF-16 for a (u) marker or from 6.3.0, not from 5.6.0: Inno
Setup 5.6.x still had ANSI builds, and innoextract's version table lists
(5.6.0) and the (5.6.2) pre-release GOG used in both forms
(setup/version.cpp). Review findings H1 and L1.

--- a/src/util/encoding.rs
+++ b/src/util/encoding.rs
@@ -90,20 +90,16 @@
 /// Decides whether a given `Version` uses UTF-16LE strings on the
 /// wire.
 ///
-/// The marker's `(u)` suffix is the most explicit signal but it is
-/// inconsistent in practice: HeidiSQL 6.4.0.1 ships an ANSI marker
-/// yet stores all strings as UTF-16LE. Inno Setup has been
-/// Unicode-by-default since 5.6 - we treat that as the rule and
-/// the marker `(u)` as an informational hint.
+/// The marker's `(u)` suffix marks a Unicode build, and from 6.3.0 every
+/// build is Unicode whatever its marker (HeidiSQL 6.4.0.1 ships an ANSI
+/// marker yet stores all strings as UTF-16LE).
+///
+/// Arcanum CE patch (gogx, 2026-10-31): the rule was `at_least(5, 6, 0)`,
+/// but 5.6.x still had ANSI builds, `(5.6.0)` and the `(5.6.2)` pre-release
+/// that GOG used; innoextract's version table lists both forms and makes an
+/// unmarked version Unicode only from 6.3.0 (setup/version.cpp).
 pub(crate) fn is_unicode_for_version(version: &Version) -> bool {
-    if version.is_unicode() {
-        return true;
-    }
-    // Inno Setup 5.6 (release 2017) made the Unicode build the
-    // default; legacy ANSI builds shipped only for 5.5 and earlier.
-    // For 5.6+ we treat the wire as Unicode regardless of the marker
-    // suffix.
-    version.at_least(5, 6, 0)
+    version.is_unicode() || version.at_least(6, 3, 0)
 }
 
